 "answer": "The main crops of the United States by harvested area are dominated by soybeans and maize, followed by wheat, cotton, and sorghum [S1]. \n\nSoya beans rank first with 34,330,527 hectares, covering 34.74% of the harvested area [S1].\n\nMaize (corn) ranks second with 33,613,081 hectares, covering 34.01% of the harvested area [S1].\n\nWheat ranks third with 15,004,017 hectares, covering 15.18% of the harvested area [S1].\n\nSeed cotton, unginned covers 3,052,090 hectares (3.09% share), and sorghum covers 2,197,467 hectares (2.22% share) [S1].",
